# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Ivo Neefjes et al. (2026). Machine learning interatomic potentials with accurate long-range interactions for molecular dynamics collision simulations of atmospherically-relevant molecules.
#   Atmospheric chemistry and physics. doi:10.5194/acp-26-7631-2026
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 446dedcdba7495cc...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 457 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/neefjes2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: per-system training sets (20,000 structures each from
# GFN1-xTB collision and umbrella-sampling MD, labelled with GFN1-xTB or
# wB97X-3c) for H2SO4-H2SO4, H2SO4-NH(CH3)2 and H2SO4-HSO4-, AIMNet2,
# PaiNN and Delta-PaiNN (correction to GFN1-xTB) models trained on them,
# and their energy and force MAEs on independent test sets (Table 3).
# PMF RMSEs (Table 4) and collision rate coefficients (Table 5) are
# properties.

